# Helm Practice & Cluster Addons Guide (CKA)

This directory contains standalone Helm automation scripts designed for hands-on Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) practice with package management, cluster monitoring, and metrics addons.

---

## 1. Directory Structure

```text
/home/vagrant/cka/helm/
├── README.md                      # This guide
├── install-kube-metrics.sh        # Metrics Server Helm installer (--kubelet-insecure-tls)
├── install-kube-prometheus.sh     # Lightweight Prometheus Operator installer (Prometheus only)
└── install-nginx-gateway-fabric.sh # NGINX Gateway Fabric installer (Gateway API)
```

---

## 2. Overview of Addon Scripts

| Script | Helm Chart | Target Namespace | Description & Footprint |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `install-kube-metrics.sh` | `metrics-server/metrics-server` | `kube-system` | Enables `kubectl top nodes` and `kubectl top pods`. Configured with `--kubelet-insecure-tls` for homelab kubelet scraping. |
| `install-kube-prometheus.sh` | `prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack` | `monitoring` | Deploys Prometheus Operator and a single-replica Prometheus instance. Grafana, Alertmanager, node-exporter, and kube-state-metrics are disabled for a minimal footprint on lab VMs. |
| `install-nginx-gateway-fabric.sh` | `oci://ghcr.io/nginx/charts/nginx-gateway-fabric` | `nginx-gateway` | Deploys NGINX Gateway Fabric and standard Kubernetes Gateway API CRDs (`gatewayclasses`, `gateways`, `httproutes`). Configured with `NodePort` service type for lab VM accessibility. |

---

## 3. Usage Instructions

### Script 1: Install Kubernetes Metrics Server

Run the installer:

```bash
cd /home/vagrant/cka/helm
./install-kube-metrics.sh
```

#### Verification

Wait 60–90 seconds for initial metric gathering, then run:

```bash
# Verify Metrics Server deployment
kubectl get deployment metrics-server -n kube-system

# Verify node metrics collection
kubectl top nodes

# Verify pod metrics collection across all namespaces
kubectl top pods -A
```

#### Uninstallation

```bash
helm uninstall metrics-server -n kube-system
```

---

### Script 2: Install Minimal Prometheus Operator

Run the installer:

```bash
cd /home/vagrant/cka/helm
./install-kube-prometheus.sh
```

#### Verification

```bash
# Verify Prometheus operator and instance pods
kubectl get pods -n monitoring

# Verify Prometheus custom resource
kubectl get prometheus -n monitoring

# Verify registered ServiceMonitors
kubectl get servicemonitors -A
```

#### Accessing Prometheus Web UI

Forward the Prometheus server port to localhost:

```bash
kubectl port-forward -n monitoring svc/kube-prometheus-kube-prome-prometheus 9090:9090
```

From another terminal or via curl:

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:9090/-/ready
```

#### Uninstallation

```bash
helm uninstall kube-prometheus -n monitoring
kubectl delete namespace monitoring
```

---

### Script 3: Install NGINX Gateway Fabric

Run the installer:

```bash
cd /home/vagrant/cka/helm
./install-nginx-gateway-fabric.sh
```

#### Verification

```bash
# Verify Gateway API CRDs
kubectl get crds | grep -i gateway

# Verify GatewayClass registered by controller
kubectl get gatewayclasses

# Verify NGINX Gateway Fabric deployment and service (NodePorts 30080/30443)
kubectl get pods,svc -n nginx-gateway

# Test connectivity from control plane or workstation on host/NodePort 30080
curl -I http://192.168.56.20:30080/
```

#### Uninstallation

```bash
helm uninstall ngf -n nginx-gateway
kubectl delete namespace nginx-gateway
```

